<article class="env-lemma" id="0B03">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0B03">Lemma <span data-tag="0B03">43.16.2</span>.</a> Let $A$ be a Noetherian local ring. Let $I = (f_1, \ldots , f_ r)$ be an ideal generated by a regular sequence. Let $M$ be a finite $A$-module. Assume that $\dim (\text{Supp}(M/IM)) = 0$. Then </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  e_ I(M, r) = \sum (-1)^ i\text{length}_ A(\text{Tor}_ i^ A(A/I, M))  \]
</div>
  <p> Here $e_ I(M, r)$ is as in Remark <a href="/tag/0B00" data-tag="0B00">43.15.6</a>. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Since $f_1, \ldots , f_ r$ is a regular sequence the Koszul complex $K_\bullet (f_1, \ldots , f_ r)$ is a resolution of $A/I$ over $A$, see More on Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/09CC" data-tag="09CC">15.31.7</a>. Thus the right hand side is equal to 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \sum (-1)^ i\text{length}_ A H_ i(K_\bullet (f_1, \ldots , f_ r) \otimes _ A M)  \]
</div>
    <p>
       Now the result follows immediately from Theorem <a href="/tag/0AZZ" data-tag="0AZZ">43.15.5</a> if $I$ is an ideal of definition. In general, we replace $A$ by $\overline{A} = A/\text{Ann}(M)$ and $f_1, \ldots , f_ r$ by $\overline{f}_1, \ldots , \overline{f}_ r$ which is allowed because 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  K_\bullet (f_1, \ldots , f_ r) \otimes _ A M = K_\bullet (\overline{f}_1, \ldots , \overline{f}_ r) \otimes _{\overline{A}} M  \]
</div>
    <p>
       Since $e_ I(M, r) = e_{\overline{I}}(M, r)$ where $\overline{I} = (\overline{f}_1, \ldots , \overline{f}_ r) \subset \overline{A}$ is an ideal of definition the result follows from Theorem <a href="/tag/0AZZ" data-tag="0AZZ">43.15.5</a> in this case as well. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>